WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:55.800
Well, Straw Hat Luffy, this is a good way to die.

3
00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.390
<b>Croc-ish</b>

4
00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.480
Within six minutes,
this yard will be blown up

5
00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.410
along with the Square.

6
00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.850
I'd stay, but I'm in a hurry.

7
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.450
You just wait right there, okay?

8
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.390
And then you can celebrate the
new king of the sand country.

9
00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.780
Now then...

10
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.550
I should be on my way.

11
00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:23.110
He said it's in the mortuary
temple to the west of here.

12
00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.730
Missed me.

13
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.880
Ah! That was way too close.

14
00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.150
That bastard! He took off!

15
00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.860
I think he flew off in that direction.

16
00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:01.390
He won't get away
with this! Damn him!

17
00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:05.080
<b>Mortuary Temple
(Royal Mausoleum)
West of the Palace</b>

18
00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.100
So this is the royal tomb.

19
00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:19.180
Where generations of your kings
lay in their eternal rest.

20
00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:22.190
So, where's the Poneglyph?

21
00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:36.480
Hidden stairs.

22
00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:41.210
The Poneglyph is kept
down there, deep underground.

23
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.420
Most people aren't even aware
of the Poneglyph's existence.

24
00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.820
Many events occur behind the scenes.

25
00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.450
Just because a country belongs
to the World Government

26
00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:53.290
doesn't necessarily mean that
its king knows what's going on.

27
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.330
You shouldn't be blamed.

28
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.800
Like most people, you probably had no idea

29
00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.230
there was someone
left in the world

30
00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.700
who can decipher
the ancient writing.

31
00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.530
You can actually read Poneglyphs?

32
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.800
That's right.

33
00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.320
That's why Crocodile and I ended
up as a team in the first place.

34
00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.260
It's also why he can't
kill me. I'm no use dead.

35
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.460
Tell me, is it correct

36
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.730
that the Poneglyph in this
country tells where Pluton is?

37
00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.240
Is that really the case?

38
00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.740
Alabasta's royal family has been obligated

39
00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.850
for generations now to protect it.

40
00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.480
That duty is about the only thing we know about it.

41
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.720
Protect? Don't make me laugh.

42
00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.490
This place is quite impressive.

43
00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.700
It's located behind
the doors in the back.

44
00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.810
There it is.

45
00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.030
This way!

46
00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.840
Now you die!

47
00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:02.980
What are you doing?!

48
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.110
What am I doing?

49
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.160
I'm trying to get inside Crocodile's head, that's what!

50
00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:07.160
Like, if I were him,

51
00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.180
where would I wanna
shoot a cannon from?

52
00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.520
Just keep looking!
We only have five minutes!

53
00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.330
Five minutes to go
before a million people all die!

54
00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:15.820
We really need to hurry!

55
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.330
We don't have much time
left to find the cannon!

56
00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.930
Chopper, do you think you can
find the guy by using your nose?

57
00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.000
That won't work.

58
00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.170
The only thing I can smell
anywhere is gunpowder!

59
00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.300
We have to do something!

60
00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.440
Try finding the smell of a guy

61
00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.840
who's about to blow up the
Square with a big cannon.

62
00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.140
What kinda smell is that?

63
00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.040
How should I know? Just try it!

64
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.760
A cannonball that can
blow up that big an area.

65
00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:43.030
Hold on, in that case,
it's gotta be really big.

66
00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:44.530
And if it's gonna be
shot out of a cannon,

67
00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.400
then surely can't go very far.

68
00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.860
So it's gotta be closer
to the Square than this!

69
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.600
There's no way I have time to go around!

70
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.880
There! A shortcut!

71
00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.440
Anything from the sky, Pell?

72
00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.310
I searched every
rooftop near the Square,

73
00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:01.400
but I couldn't see any
sign of a cannon.

74
00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:04.600
Well then, it might be in a building somewhere.

75
00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.000
Right. I'll search them all.

76
00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.130
Good!

77
00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:20.880
How many times must you try this

78
00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.880
before giving up?

79
00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.020
Crocodile, it's you.

80
00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.060
Looks like Nico
Robin made short work of you.

81
00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.890
I must say, I never
thought the Marines

82
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.720
would follow me to this city.

83
00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.130
Where's your boss?

84
00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:48.670
Did that smoky idiot run away
and leave you all alone?

85
00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.010
Justice is only for the people who take it.

86
00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.480
That's the kind of world we live in, girl.

87
00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.010
Why don't you just go back to
your base and talk about justice

88
00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.480
until you're actually
ready to fight for it?

89
00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.540
Crocodile.

90
00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:23.110
Straw Hat!

91
00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:26.310
Where'd he go? Where?

92
00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:30.770
Tell me right now!
Which way did he go?

93
00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.680
Towards the temple. That way.

94
00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.480
That direction? Thank you!

95
00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.800
What justice is there?

96
00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:16.900
To hell with
Marine Headquarters.

97
00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.300
Jeez. I can't move very well.

98
00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:33.570
This is strange.
I ate all that meat.

99
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.500
What's wrong? These
wounds are small.

100
00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:40.340
I wonder... if I
should lie down.

101
00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:44.440
Well, did it tell you everything

102
00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.050
that you wanted to know?

103
00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:58.270
Now I see it. Secret stairs.

104
00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.330
Just four more minutes.

105
00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.660
Aren't there any others around?

106
00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.090
Is this all that your country is hiding?

107
00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.760
You aren't satisfied?

108
00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:37.900
I have kept every word of the promise I made to you.

109
00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:38.930
You did.

110
00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.040
Just like any
other national secret.

111
00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.210
No matter how hard you look,

112
00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:49.870
you can't find it unless you already know where it is.

113
00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:54.470
So this is the Poneglyph
we were looking for.

114
00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.160
That didn't take much time.

115
00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.870
Now that you have this odd thing in front of you,

116
00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.040
were you able to decipher it?

117
00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.240
Yes.

118
00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:07.010
Very good. Now read it aloud.
What does this thing say?

119
00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.850
"Kahira conquered Alabasta

120
00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.980
in Sky Ephemeris Year 239.

121
00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:19.300
In year 260, Taymer
ruled the Bitain Dynasty.

122
00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:24.140
In year 306, the Taff Cathedral
was completed in Erumalu.

123
00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:26.970
In year 325, the hero
Mamdin of Oltia..."

124
00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:28.840
Hey, hold on. What's this?

125
00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:31.150
Is this really all the information here?

126
00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.870
I don't give a damn about this desert's history!

127
00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.840
I want to know about the world's
most dangerous military power

128
00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:38.470
that's hiding in this country.

129
00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.270
Where is the Pluton hidden?

130
00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:43.450
That information isn't on here.

131
00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.550
What?

132
00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.950
History is the only thing that this text contains.

133
00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:47.950
That's all?

134
00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:51.260
Pluton, I didn't
see it anywhere.

135
00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.190
It isn't mentioned on
this Poneglyph at all.

136
00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:57.840
Not mentioned at all. I see.

137
00:10:57.870 --> 00:10:59.980
That's unfortunate.

138
00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:03.180
You've been an excellent
partner, but even so,

139
00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:05.950
I think that I'll kill
you right here.

140
00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.620
What?

141
00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:08.850
The agreement that we made

142
00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:11.260
four years ago has
been fulfilled.

143
00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.700
Do you remember the terms of that agreement?

144
00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.800
I was to bring you to the
Poneglyph, and in turn,

145
00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.990
you would hand over the
information on the weapon to me.

146
00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.760
The work you've done for Baroque Works

147
00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.060
these past four years
was excellent

148
00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:28.730
both in terms of intellect
and your ability to command.

149
00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:31.270
Your usefulness to the company
has been reason enough

150
00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:32.980
to keep you around.

151
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.770
But in the end, you've spoiled it all...

152
00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:38.940
...by betraying me, Nico Robin.

153
00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.270
You say the Poneglyph
in this country

154
00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.080
doesn't say anything at all about Pluton.

155
00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:47.310
Is that true?

156
00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:50.680
Was this the plan all along,
to hide the information from me

157
00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.880
even if you were able to
find something useful?

158
00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:01.680
But even so, I don't
feel any anger toward you,

159
00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:05.160
and do you know why
that is, Nico Robin?

160
00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:06.360
Heh. All right.

161
00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.890
I've worked with you for four years.

162
00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.660
I knew you'd try something like this someday,

163
00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.400
so I'm more than ready.

164
00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.400
Water.

165
00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:16.830
If you get wet, then a knife should go right into you!

166
00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:19.940
Damn it. Where'd he go?

167
00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:29.100
Now all is forgiven, Nico Robin.

168
00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.270
Because I never trusted you.

169
00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.180
From the very beginning
of our partnership,

170
00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.750
I knew better than to do something as foolish as that.

171
00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:49.420
I can tell from Cobra's reaction

172
00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.220
that Pluton really does exist.

173
00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.930
I don't need the Poneglyph.
I can find the Pluton on my own.

174
00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:59.700
Once this country is mine, it's only a matter of time.

175
00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:02.710
What's happening?

176
00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.890
It's still too early for
the attack on the Square.

177
00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:08.690
It must be you. What did you do?

178
00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.920
It's just a little present.

179
00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:12.820
You see, this underground temple was built

180
00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.920
so that disturbing just one small column

181
00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:17.190
will destroy the balance
of the entire structure

182
00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:18.970
and cause it to collapse.

183
00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:21.300
The two of you are going to die here.

184
00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:22.970
We'll meet death together.

185
00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:26.340
I am the 12th king of
the Nefertari family.

186
00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:27.980
I will uphold our honor.

187
00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.750
Someone like you could
never be allowed

188
00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:33.220
to rule the desert kingdom.

189
00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:37.780
Impressive. You truly
are a model king.

190
00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:40.980
Willing to give your own life
just to take me down with you,

191
00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.120
for your kingdom.

192
00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.620
Except, I won't die.

193
00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:46.590
Huh?

194
00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:48.820
All I have to do is
change the rocks to sand

195
00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.180
and I can escape from here.

196
00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.700
Your death will be in vain, Cobra.

197
00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.530
There are only three minutes left.

198
00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:00.170
When the square blows up and this temple collapses,

199
00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:04.170
everyone standing in my way will
be eliminated in an instant.

200
00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.810
And in that moment, this land...

201
00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.480
...will become mine entirely.

202
00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.440
Three minutes left. Where is it?

203
00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.840
A cannon big enough to
destroy such a large area

204
00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.440
has to be enormous.

205
00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:41.180
There can't be many places to hide such a weapon.

206
00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:45.410
So why are we still unable to find it after all this?

207
00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.020
An open space where
a cannon would fit...

208
00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:51.010
Ah! Stop shooting!

209
00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:52.980
Open space!

210
00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.670
That's not fair, Koza.

211
00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.970
Hiding in a place like this the entire time?

212
00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.580
Yeah, Leader, no fair!

213
00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:03.080
Yes! That place would work!

214
00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:05.790
That's dangerous! I told
you to stop shooting at me!

215
00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:06.690
Taste Smoke Star!

216
00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.960
It's perfect. It's
hidden and it's big.

217
00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.560
I told you I'm not
from the rebel army!

218
00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.830
Usopp Hammer!

219
00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.860
Usopp Rubberband of Doom!

220
00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.730
That should teach ya!

221
00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.800
Do they know who they're
dealing with here?1

222
00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.080
Don't be afraid when I tell
you this...no, be very afraid!

223
00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:25.810
I am the incredible
Captain Usopp.

224
00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:26.750
What? Oh, it's you, Vivi.

225
00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.620
So, were you able to
find the cannoneer?

226
00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.520
I know now. I've figured it out!

227
00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:32.900
What? You know where?

228
00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:34.100
There it is.

229
00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:35.830
I'll go ahead and signal everyone.

230
00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:38.670
You're sure about this, right?

231
00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:43.510
Special Attack:
Red Serpent Star!

232
00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:21.010
Ah, I slept good!

233
00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:21.380
Wait.

234
00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:22.350
Oh, that's right.

235
00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:23.420
I couldn't move all of a sudden

236
00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.950
so I decided to risk it
and take a nap right here

237
00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:28.890
since there was really
no other choice.

238
00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.860
Yeah. And I feel better now.

239
00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:33.520
So...

240
00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.390
Oh, right! Time for me
to beat up Crocodile!

241
00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:49.680
That hole over
there looks kinda...

242
00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.650
...kinda croc-ish.

243
00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:58.770
What's with this freaky
place, anyway?

244
00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.880
The whole thing is crumbling into pieces!

245
00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:14.750
I'm certain of it!
The cannon has to be in there.

246
00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.520
I can't think of any other options besides that place.

247
00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.690
What makes you so sure that
it's in there, anyway, Vivi?

248
00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.090
We have to assume
that this dust devil

249
00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.060
is part of the plan.

250
00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:25.260
The cannon must be in a place

251
00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.590
where they can still see well
enough to hit the target.

252
00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.170
Also, it has to be an open space
where a cannon can fit,

253
00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.840
but where it can't be
seen from the sky.

254
00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.770
This place is
big enough, isn't it?

255
00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.710
So then, let's make it
the clan's secret base!

256
00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.740
What do ya say?

257
00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:43.980
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

258
00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.510
So that has to be it!

259
00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:46.890
It makes perfect sense to me.

260
00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.190
Okay, hold on.

261
00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:50.350
We'll leave the others a message
since they're headed this way.

262
00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:53.020
Thanks, Usopp. I'm going
ahead to the tower.

263
00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:55.340
Hey! Wait, Vivi! Wait!

264
00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.080
Hurry!

265
00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:56.820
Right.

266
00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:58.190
Well, look at that!

267
00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:01.130
It's the princess.
We found her, boys!

268
00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:05.630
Yeah, that was just too easy.
The signal led us right to her.

269
00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:08.930
There are more members of
the Baroque Works Billions.

270
00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:12.870
Oh, no! We signaled
the enemy, too!

271
00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:15.640
That smoke. It's Usopp's signal.
He must've found it.

272
00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:18.840
Okay. But why's the
palace so far away?

273
00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:21.780
Good. It's not far from here.

274
00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.680
I wonder if that signal means
that they found the cannoneer.

275
00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.950
They must have. Let's go!

276
00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:32.790
Now! Noisy Attack!

277
00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.500
Ha-ha!

278
00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.230
Tremble at the
power of my nails!

279
00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.470
Come on, Vivi! Let's go.

280
00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.800
Yeah.

281
00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:46.570
Hey, over there! Get 'em!

282
00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:10.790
So, it's you.

283
00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:14.920
You can't get away. You're mine!

284
00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.930
How are you still alive?

285
00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.060
No matter how many times I kill you,

286
00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.430
you just keep coming
back for more.

287
00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.900
Well? Answer me, brat!

288
00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.400
How'd he do it?

289
00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:30.410
How did he live and come
here? Who is this boy?

290
00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.310
It's Straw Hat.

291
00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:43.780
Tell me, just how many times do you have to die?

292
00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:46.380
There's something you still
need to return, Crocodile.

293
00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.980
And I came here to get it back.

294
00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.910
What is this thing I took?

295
00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:54.720
Is it money? Is it fame?

296
00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:58.520
Or people's trust? Their lives?

297
00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.490
Is it rain?

298
00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:03.570
I have taken all
of those things.

299
00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:09.730
So which is it that you want me to give back, Straw Hat?

300
00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:11.780
This land.

301
00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:12.720
The land?

302
00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:15.190
Really, you should know better than that by now.

303
00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.060
I have no intention of relinquishing this country.

304
00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.130
Why would I, when
I'm going to become

305
00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:23.160
its next king before long?

306
00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.460
We came to this island to save Vivi's country.

307
00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.470
But then, when we got here, it was gone.

308
00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:30.970
You stole her country!

309
00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.870
I have to get to the rebel army.

310
00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.560
I must persuade their leader

311
00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:41.920
to stop all of this
pointless bloodshed.

312
00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:43.560
Up until a few short years ago,

313
00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.660
it was a thriving city
full of gardens,

314
00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.830
and palm trees,
and lush greenery.

315
00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:51.500
Please, Vivi!

316
00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:56.870
You have to stop these fools from tearing our country apart!

317
00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:57.770
This is her country,

318
00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:00.620
and I'm here to take
it back from you.

319
00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.730
And what's wrong with that?

320
00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:05.650
What's so very wrong about
not wanting to see people die?

321
00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:07.520
Just being in this
country one day

322
00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:12.090
and taking one a look
around, even I can tell...

323
00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:15.780
...what this country
needs more than anything!

324
00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:18.080
You think that putting
just your life on the line

325
00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.170
is enough to stop
this from happening?

326
00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:21.660
What, Luffy?

327
00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:24.160
I don't have anything else I can put on the line.

328
00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:28.920
Just... Just me.

329
00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:32.160
Well, you can at least try
putting all of our lives

330
00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.910
on the line together!

331
00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:36.410
Aren't we friends?! Huh?!

332
00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:45.020
I will defeat you and take this
country out of your evil hands.

333
00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:48.960
And then, Vivi will smile again!

334
00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.130
Threaten me as much as you like,

335
00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.700
but without any water, you're nothing.

336
00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:07.740
This is impossible.

337
00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:12.110
He doesn't have any water,
so how can he kick me?

338
00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:16.850
This is your fault, you monster!

339
00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:19.480
This country would be peaceful if it weren't for you!

340
00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:23.420
It's heartbreaking, isn't it?

341
00:22:23.420 --> 00:22:25.460
Their love for the kingdom...

342
00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:28.430
...will be what destroys it.

343
00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:38.800
No!

344
00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:56.650
I see. You're using...
your blood.

345
00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:59.320
Clever.

346
00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:03.660
Blood can harden sand, too, can't it?

347
00:23:13.670 --> 00:23:16.310
First Rainbase,
and then the royal palace,

348
00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:19.890
and now this underground temple.

349
00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:24.680
You should be rewarded for your
insistence on challenging me.

350
00:23:24.740 --> 00:23:27.240
Even after I've put you through hell twice now,

351
00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:28.010
you keep on coming back.

352
00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.250
Why, you!

353
00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:36.410
You're a pirate, Straw Hat.

354
00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.710
You've certainly proven
that in your determination

355
00:23:38.740 --> 00:23:41.210
to defeat me no matter the cost.

356
00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:42.480
And I'll admit that
you've become

357
00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:44.260
an annoyingly
persistent opponent

358
00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:46.630
during our three encounters.

359
00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:50.030
All right. What's that?

360
00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:51.940
A poisonous hook.

361
00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:52.940
I see.

362
00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:55.970
You seem to be a competent pirate, I suppose.

363
00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:57.940
So surely, you must understand

364
00:23:57.940 --> 00:24:00.440
that a duel between
pirates is always about

365
00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.710
two people fighting
for survival.

366
00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:03.960
And when that's the case,

367
00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:07.330
there's no such thing as playing dirty.

368
00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:15.790
When the explosion happens in the Square,

369
00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:18.900
this place will most likely crumble to dust.

370
00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:20.830
This will be our final battle,

371
00:24:20.900 --> 00:24:24.040
so let's settle this once and for all!

372
00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:29.780
The smoke was coming
from this direction, wasn't it?

373
00:24:31.390 --> 00:24:33.290
Or was it? Argh.

374
00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:36.390
Wha...? The Marines?

375
00:24:36.460 --> 00:24:38.330
Hey, look. It's Roronoa Zoro.

376
00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.460
Just great.

377
00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:41.630
I didn't realize the Marines were in this town now.

378
00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:44.000
I don't have time for this.

379
00:24:44.020 --> 00:24:45.160
Oh, damn it.

380
00:24:45.190 --> 00:24:47.330
I guess I have no choice but to deal with them quickly.

381
00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:49.630
Why are you here in the middle of the battlefield?

382
00:24:49.660 --> 00:24:51.230
Yeah, what do you think you're doing here?

383
00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:53.630
Well, I could say the
same thing to you!

384
00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:54.800
Hold it, Zoro!

385
00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:55.770
Go that way.

386
00:24:55.770 --> 00:24:57.270
If you head north at the next corner,

387
00:24:57.270 --> 00:24:59.100
then you can reach the Palace Square.

388
00:24:59.100 --> 00:25:01.270
Go back and turn right!
It's not this way!

389
00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:02.840
Are you that stupid?

390
00:25:02.870 --> 00:25:03.840
Stupid?

391
00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:04.780
Get outta here!

392
00:25:04.810 --> 00:25:05.780
Go!

393
00:25:05.810 --> 00:25:06.810
Uh. What the...? How di...?

394
00:25:06.810 --> 00:25:10.380
Faster! We have to
run faster, Vivi!

395
00:25:10.380 --> 00:25:11.620
I don't think I can, Usopp!

396
00:25:11.650 --> 00:25:15.220
Don't let the princess get away!
Our promotions are on the line.

397
00:25:17.720 --> 00:25:19.120
Huh?

398
00:25:31.170 --> 00:25:33.400
Uh... Thank you?

399
00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:35.340
We're here to help you, not fight!

400
00:25:35.410 --> 00:25:37.780
Go stop the explosion
in the Square, okay?

401
00:25:37.810 --> 00:25:38.640
Now go, quickly!

402
00:25:38.680 --> 00:25:41.250
Let's get going Usopp.
Come on, hurry.

403
00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:44.080
– Right!
– Thank you!

404
00:25:56.560 --> 00:25:58.790
Hurry! We have to hurry!

405
00:25:58.830 --> 00:26:00.330
We've wasted a lot of time!

406
00:26:00.360 --> 00:26:02.300
I don't know why they
helped us back there,

407
00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:03.330
but if it weren't
for the Marines,

408
00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:05.800
we'd be a lot worse off now!

409
00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:17.810
No, don't look at that!

410
00:26:17.820 --> 00:26:18.870
We don't have time to help them!

411
00:26:18.870 --> 00:26:19.840
If we don't stop the explosion,

412
00:26:19.870 --> 00:26:22.880
the casualties will be a lot worse than that!

413
00:26:22.910 --> 00:26:24.110
Right.

414
00:26:24.300 --> 00:26:27.470
Crying about it isn't gonna
stop the attack from happening!

415
00:26:31.420 --> 00:26:33.360
In two minutes,
we're either gonna beat them,

416
00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:34.450
or we're gonna die.

417
00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:36.020
We still have time left!

418
00:26:36.060 --> 00:26:36.860
Yes!

419
00:26:36.860 --> 00:26:38.360
And we're all helping you!

420
00:26:38.390 --> 00:26:39.860
Yes!

421
00:26:44.280 --> 00:26:47.550
Right there! Vivi! Usopp!

422
00:26:47.550 --> 00:26:50.120
It's Nami! And Tony!

423
00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:51.050
What's going on?

424
00:26:51.080 --> 00:26:53.050
The Marines just helped us out back there!

425
00:26:53.050 --> 00:26:55.020
Were you able to find
where the cannon is?

426
00:26:55.020 --> 00:26:56.020
We haven't confirmed it yet,

427
00:26:56.020 --> 00:26:58.430
but that's this is the
only place it can be!

428
00:26:58.460 --> 00:27:01.400
We must've passed it a bunch
of times before I realized it.

429
00:27:01.430 --> 00:27:05.300
The cannon is up there.
I'm absolutely sure of it now.

430
00:27:08.430 --> 00:27:09.660
The clock tower?

431
00:27:11.550 --> 00:27:12.780
I see.

432
00:27:12.780 --> 00:27:15.150
From up there, he can get a
really good shot at the Square.

433
00:27:15.180 --> 00:27:17.120
We still need Pell to get here, though.

434
00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:19.540
It's the only way to stop it.

435
00:27:19.570 --> 00:27:21.140
Pell.

436
00:27:29.980 --> 00:27:32.550
We don't have much time.

437
00:27:32.580 --> 00:27:34.420
I could've sworn I saw
the smoke coming up

438
00:27:34.480 --> 00:27:37.190
from somewhere around this area.

439
00:27:37.670 --> 00:27:39.670
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

440
00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:40.840
Did you see that?

441
00:27:40.870 --> 00:27:44.270
I just shot down that big bird
with my Ribbit-Ribbit Gun.

442
00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:45.610
Quite impressive, huh?

443
00:27:51.010 --> 00:27:52.720
I'm sorry.

444
00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:58.610
Gum-Gum Pistol!

445
00:29:44.150 --> 00:29:47.720
He's so strong.
Who in the world is he?

446
00:29:47.750 --> 00:29:51.150
Crocodile made even our best
warriors look like children.

447
00:29:51.220 --> 00:29:54.060
But now, he's
actually struggling.

448
00:30:00.730 --> 00:30:05.270
You were skewered,
buried alive, and dried up.

449
00:30:06.750 --> 00:30:08.180
You may have made it through all that,

450
00:30:08.250 --> 00:30:11.320
but you won't escape this time, Straw Hat.

451
00:30:11.380 --> 00:30:13.180
There's no hope for survival.

452
00:30:13.210 --> 00:30:15.050
The game is over.

453
00:30:15.110 --> 00:30:18.120
This poison will spread through you soon.

454
00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:21.540
You know, Crocodile?
You just don't understand.

455
00:30:21.540 --> 00:30:23.780
I wonder what happened.

456
00:30:26.390 --> 00:30:29.890
Pell? I don't see him
up there anywhere.

457
00:30:29.890 --> 00:30:30.820
But I don't think there's
any way that we can get

458
00:30:30.820 --> 00:30:33.320
to the top of the tower in less
than a minute without any help.

459
00:30:34.800 --> 00:30:36.930
Pell, where are you?
Hurry. We need you.

460
00:30:36.960 --> 00:30:39.740
For now, we're going to have
to get moving without him.

461
00:30:39.770 --> 00:30:41.600
We're gonna have to climb
all these use the stairs.

462
00:30:41.660 --> 00:30:42.760
You guys ready?

463
00:30:42.900 --> 00:30:44.070
Hey!

464
00:30:44.100 --> 00:30:44.800
– Huh?
– Huh?

465
00:30:44.870 --> 00:30:47.700
Nami! Hey, Vivi!

466
00:30:47.740 --> 00:30:50.110
Sanji, what are you
doing all the way up there?

467
00:30:50.140 --> 00:30:51.160
What do you think?

468
00:30:51.160 --> 00:30:54.830
You left a message where the smoke was, didn't you?

469
00:30:54.830 --> 00:30:56.730
The message said
"Go to the clock tower,"

470
00:30:56.760 --> 00:30:59.340
so I figured I'd better head up here to meet you.

471
00:30:59.340 --> 00:31:00.780
So what should I do?

472
00:31:00.810 --> 00:31:02.480
Where's the cannoneer, anyway?

473
00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:04.570
The top! He's at the top!

474
00:31:04.570 --> 00:31:07.340
Go up from there and take him down!

475
00:31:07.410 --> 00:31:09.240
Sanji?

476
00:31:09.280 --> 00:31:11.680
Hey! Where were you?
I was looking!

477
00:31:11.760 --> 00:31:13.690
Zoro! You're here, too?

478
00:31:13.760 --> 00:31:15.600
What are you doin' down there?

479
00:31:15.720 --> 00:31:17.720
Funny, I was gonna
ask you the same thing!

480
00:31:17.760 --> 00:31:18.620
It was the Marines.

481
00:31:18.700 --> 00:31:20.640
They kept saying
"go north, go north,"

482
00:31:20.690 --> 00:31:23.530
so I just kept going north till
I got all the way up here.

483
00:31:23.570 --> 00:31:25.710
"North" and "up"
aren't the same thing!

484
00:31:25.710 --> 00:31:27.710
Anyway, good job, you two!

485
00:31:27.710 --> 00:31:29.380
Now just keep on going up from there

486
00:31:29.410 --> 00:31:30.910
and destroy the clock tower, okay?

487
00:31:30.910 --> 00:31:32.580
No way!

488
00:31:32.660 --> 00:31:34.430
They can't get inside
the clock tower

489
00:31:34.500 --> 00:31:35.530
from where they are now.

490
00:31:35.570 --> 00:31:37.670
You see, there are
only two ways in:

491
00:31:37.680 --> 00:31:40.080
The back stairs on the first
floor and from the sky.

492
00:31:40.150 --> 00:31:41.820
That's why we need Pell!

493
00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:43.010
But can't Zoro just go ahead

494
00:31:43.010 --> 00:31:44.710
and destroy the wall
or something?

495
00:31:44.740 --> 00:31:45.580
We can't risk that.

496
00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:46.970
It could make the cannonball explode

497
00:31:46.970 --> 00:31:48.640
even earlier for all we know.

498
00:31:48.740 --> 00:31:51.050
We have no choice but to take the stairs.

499
00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:53.580
No, wait. Vivi!

500
00:31:53.620 --> 00:31:55.980
I think I have a better plan.

501
00:32:00.560 --> 00:32:02.560
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit...

502
00:32:10.800 --> 00:32:12.470
So, Mr. 7,

503
00:32:12.540 --> 00:32:14.410
according to what
the boss told us,

504
00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:17.370
this is going to be our final
mission for Baroque Works.

505
00:32:17.410 --> 00:32:18.810
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

506
00:32:18.080 --> 00:32:24.260
<b>Mr. 7

Frontier Agent
Baroque Works Ms. Father's Day

Frontier Agent
Baroque Works</b>

507
00:32:20.680 --> 00:32:22.080
That's right, Miss Father's Day.

508
00:32:24.520 --> 00:32:27.560
According to the plan, we have
just 30 seconds left to go.

509
00:32:28.170 --> 00:32:29.640
Who are they?

510
00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:35.700
Mr. 7 and Miss Father's Day!
